<i><b>Upgrade Notes</b></i>

* Requires NSP v1.47.1 or newer

<b>V2.35.1 Release</b>

<i><b>Features</b></i>

* Added <b>Intake Air Temperature Pre-Intercooler Differential</b> channel which will calculate the temperature difference pre/post intercooler, falling back to standard air temperature when no <i>Intake Air Temperature</i> sensor is present.

* <b>Generic Output 1-3</b> - Added third axis in the table configuration menu.

* When using NSP V1.47.0 or newer, there will now be a button in NSP to calibrate all enabled vehicle speed sensors simultaneously.

* Supports separate Day and Night Needle Images for dial gauges.

* Added <b>Speedometer (Discrete)</b> function to support pulse driven speedometers in some factory clusters.

* <b>Electrical Load</b> now supports the voltage input type, so the vehicle's electrical load current can be monitored.

<i><b>Fixes</b></i>

* Fixes the issue with populating data from CAN bus for some vendor specific ECUs.

* Updated default <i>Duty Cycle</i> for <b>Generic Output</b> options to 50%.

* <b>Generic Output</b> Tables no longer show up when using <i>input switch</i> mode.

* Fixes Dash Channel values enumeration.

* Fixes Dash not sending correct button states to ECU.

* Fixes Missing Haltech CAN Channel <i>Fuel Flow Estimated</i> support.

* Fixes Dash Generic Output value flickering when enabled in ECU.

* Fixed Peak value settings in map upgrade for Dash.

* Fixes the issue with raising false error on the virtual outputs.

* Fixed an issue where dash was not inquiring the data for PIDs of above 32 from OBDII server device.

* Fixed <b>Electrical Load Switch State</b> channel not updating.

* Resolves the problem with interpreting the input state when the input originates from an HBO channel on an external box.

* Fixes <i>Intercooler Temperature Differential</i> channel not being displayed when <i>Intake Air Temperature Pre-Intercooler</i> sensor is enabled.

* Made CAN termination come on at splash screen time (if enabled) rather than when the dash screens come up.
